    "text": "MIAMI DOLPHINSWhat's left of Miami Dolphins depth chart after Jaylen Waddle trade? Eric J. WallacePalm Beach PostUpdated March 17, 2026, 2:39 p.m. ETThe Miami Dolphins' new front office is sparing no star player in starting its organizational reconstruction.The Dolphins traded star wide receiver Jaylen Waddle, 27, to the Denver Broncos on Tuesday, March 17 in a blockbuster deal for Miami's former first round pick.Miami will reportedly receive a batch of picks in the 2026 NFL Draft picks, including the Broncos' first, third and fourth-round picks. The Dolphins also sent a fourth-round pick to the Broncos in the deal.",
